{"study_accession":"PRJNA1473344","secondary_study_accession":"SRP705882","title":"Transcriptomic analysis of GKB202-treated circulating tumor cells isolated from patients with lung cancer and pancreatic cancer","description":"Circulating tumor cells (CTCs) are associated with metastatic dissemination and adaptive stress responses in cancer. In this study, patient-derived CTCs isolated from lung cancer and pancreatic cancer samples were treated with GKB202, a natural compound derived from Antrodia cinnamomea, to investigate treatment-associated transcriptomic changes. Bulk RNA sequencing was performed to compare untreated/control and GKB202-treated CTC samples. This dataset provides raw sequencing reads and processed gene-level expression matrices for evaluating the effects of GKB202 on CTC-related transcriptional programs, including stress-response and cancer-associated pathways. Overall design: This study included matched vehicle-treated and GKB202-treated patient-derived CTC samples from lung cancer and pancreatic cancer. Lung cancer CTCs were derived from two patient samples (R24082001 and R24091001), and pancreatic cancer CTCs were derived from three patient samples (318, 414, and 531). For each matched pair, CTCs were treated with vehicle control or 2 µg/mL GKB202 for 3 days before bulk RNA sequencing. The experimental design enabled paired transcriptomic comparison of GKB202-treated CTCs against their corresponding vehicle-treated controls.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN60558547","study_accession":"PRJNA1473344","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"pancreatic CTC sample 531, GKB202-treated","description":"pancreatic CTC sample 531, GKB202-treated","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9778530","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-06-09","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","circulating tumor cells"],["treat